{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/options/01_lexical_tokens",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "options",
  "title": "Lexical tokens",
  "summary": "With `lexical` off, only what the editor's own grammar cannot tell is sent",
  "prose": "Keywords, literals, comments, built-in operators and directives are left\nto the editor's grammar. Names, template brackets, declarator operators and\nthe code of untaken branches are still sent: an inactive token without a\nkind of its own is `plain`, so the grammar's color stays and only dims.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "/// Counts the items.\ntemplate <typename T>\nint count(const T& items) {\n    int total = 0;\n    for(auto& item: items) {\n        total += 1;\n    }\n    return total; // done\n}\n\n#if 0\nint disabled = 1;\n#endif\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
